ave risen <strong class='sig'>+0.63\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.20 to +1.07) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.65\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.15 to +1.15). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 2 of 12 months. Highs rose in 1 of 12 months; July and August fell.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Rockford's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.27 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 37.2 inches a year. The wettest year was 1973 (56.48 in); the driest, 1910 (22.87 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 6 daily record highs, 2 daily record lows"}}